# Learning Agent
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your key(s):   cp .env.example .env
#
# The canonical judge scores answers with THE pinned judge model over the
# OpenAI backend (see bench/config.yaml -> judge). Put your key here so
# bench.py / the judge can call the API. The .env file is gitignored — your
# key never leaves your machine.

# REQUIRED for the canonical (reproducible) judge:
# Operator-only: raw provider keys never reach agent workspaces
# (run_sandbox.sh strips them from the seeded .env) — workspaces judge through
# the LEARNING_AGENT_JUDGE_* service below instead. Omit the line entirely if you have no
# key — the judge falls back to the logged-in claude/codex CLI (scores stamped
# canonical:false).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL alternative canonical judge backend (Anthropic Messages):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL: Weights & Biases logging for RL runs (pipeline/rl.py):
# WANDB_API_KEY=

# --- User simulator (conversational agentic tasks: tau2_*) ---
# The customer in a τ²-style task is part of the ENVIRONMENT, so dev-time and
# scored rollouts must use the SAME simulator. These two vars point at the
# operator's user-sim service (harness/user_sim.py), which pins the simulator
# model and holds the provider key itself — so unlike the keys above, they ARE
# seeded into agent workspaces. Rotate LEARNING_AGENT_USER_SIM_TOKEN to cut off access.
#   modal secret create lab-user-sim-secrets OPENAI_API_KEY=<key> LEARNING_AGENT_USER_SIM_TOKEN=<token>
#   modal app stop lab-user-sim --yes && modal deploy harness/user_sim.py
# Only the token goes here — the URL resolves from Modal automatically.
# LEARNING_AGENT_USER_SIM_TOKEN=
# LEARNING_AGENT_USER_SIM_URL=   # override only for a non-Modal deployment

# --- Judge service (ALL tasks: the one pinned judge, dev-time too) ---
# Every number that gets compared — the agent's dev-set evals, its
# intermediate-checkpoint evals during training, and official scoring — must
# come from the SAME judge. Workspaces hold no provider key, so they judge
# through the operator's judge service (harness/judge_service.py), which pins
# the judge model server-side and budgets each session. Like LEARNING_AGENT_USER_SIM_*,
# these two ARE seeded into agent workspaces; rotate the token to cut off
# access.
#   modal secret create lab-judge-secrets OPENAI_API_KEY=<key> LEARNING_AGENT_JUDGE_TOKEN=<token>
#   modal app stop lab-judge --yes && modal deploy harness/judge_service.py
# LEARNING_AGENT_JUDGE_TOKEN=
# LEARNING_AGENT_JUDGE_URL=      # the deployed service URL, ending in /v1

# Notes:
# - No key? The judge falls back to your local `claude -p` / `codex exec` CLI
#   session, but those runs are marked canonical:false in results/leaderboard
#   (uncontrolled sampling -> not comparable across machines).
# - Eval/training run on Modal and use Modal secrets (huggingface-secret etc.);
#   this file is only for the local judge + optional logging.

# --- Observatory (observability platform; see observatory/README.md) ---
# Modal environment + volume that hold all run traces/artifacts.
# MODAL_ENVIRONMENT: set to your team's shared environment to share runs;
# any personal env works solo.
MODAL_ENVIRONMENT=lab-dev
MODAL_OBS_VOLUME=lab-observatory
# Volume holding containerized agent sessions (<task>/<session>/{workspace,logs});
# used by agents/run_sandbox_modal.sh + agents/modal_runner.py:
MODAL_AGENT_VOLUME=lab-agent-workspace
# Local data dir override for developing the viewer without Modal:
# OBS_DATA_DIR=
